        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/herrick_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named for Samuel Herrick, a prominent homestead lawyer who helped open former Indian land to settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herrick%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Herrick has operated its own post office since the town was first established in 1904.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herrick%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Chicago and Northwestern Railroad arrived in 1906, facilitating the transport of crops and goods for local settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
